## 🏗️ PART 1 — Stream Kaise Banate Hain? (Creating Streams)

4 tarike hain — **SAFDG** yaad rakh (har pehle letter):

### 1️⃣ Collections se (`.stream()`) — Sabse Common!
```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.*;

List<String> names = Arrays.asList("Alice", "Bob", "Charlie", "David");

Stream<String> stream = names.stream(); // List ko Stream bana diya!

stream.forEach(System.out::println); // Print karega: Alice Bob Charlie David
```
**📝 Yaad rakh:** Koi bhi List/Set/Collection pe `.stream()` lagao — bas!

---

### 2️⃣ Array se (`Arrays.stream()`)
```java
String[] words = {"Java", "Python", "C++"};
Stream<String> wordStream = Arrays.stream(words);
wordStream.forEach(System.out::println);
```

---

### 3️⃣ `Stream.of()` — Direct Values se
```java
Stream<Integer> numberStream = Stream.of(1, 2, 3, 4, 5);
numberStream.forEach(System.out::println);
```
**📝 Yaad rakh:** Jab koi collection nahi, seedha values deni ho — `Stream.of()` use karo

---

### 4️⃣ `Stream.generate()` — Infinite Stream (Limit lagana padega!)
```java
Stream<Double> randomNumbers = Stream.generate(Math::random).limit(5);
randomNumbers.forEach(System.out::println);
```
⚠️ **`.limit(5)` zaroor lagao warna infinite loop!**

---

### 5️⃣ `Stream.iterate()` — Pattern wali Infinite Stream
```java
Stream<Integer> evenNumbers = Stream.iterate(2, n -> n + 2).limit(5);
evenNumbers.forEach(System.out::println);
// Output: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10
```
**📝 Yaad rakh:** `iterate(starting_value, lambda)` — pattern se generate karo

