## 🔧 PART 2 — Stream Operations (Dil ka Hissa!)

### 🔴 DO NOT CONFUSE: 2 Types of Operations hain

```
INTERMEDIATE Operations    →    TERMINAL Operations
(Lazy - wait karte hain)   →   (Trigger - kaam shuru hota hai)
(Return karte hain Stream) →   (Return karte hain Result/void)
Jab tak terminal nahi,     →   Yahi woh moment hai
kuch bhi execute nahi hota →   jab sab kuch chalta hai
```

---

### ⚙️ 3.1 INTERMEDIATE Operations (Stream Return Karte Hain)

Slide 6 ki table yaad rakh — **FMFDSp** (Filter, Map, FlatMap, Distinct, Sorted, peek):

| Method | Kya karta hai | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `filter()` | Condition se chhanno | Sirf even numbers |
| `map()` | Har element badlo | Lowercase → Uppercase |
| `flatMap()` | Nested list ko flat karo | `[[1,2],[3,4]]` → `[1,2,3,4]` |
| `distinct()` | Duplicates hatao | `[1,1,2,3]` → `[1,2,3]` |
| `sorted()` | Sort karo | `[5,3,1]` → `[1,3,5]` |
| `peek()` | Debugging ke liye | ForEach jaisa but stream return karta hai |

---

### 📌 Intermediate Operations — Code Examples

**🔍 filter() — Even Numbers Nikalo (Slide 7)**
```java
List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6);
numbers.stream()
       .filter(n -> n % 2 == 0)  // sirf even lo
       .forEach(System.out::println); // Output: 2, 4, 6
```
**Yaad rakh:** `filter` = **chhan-ni** — jo condition pass kare woh aage jaaye

---

**🔄 map() — Transform Elements (Slide 7)**
```java
List<String> names = Arrays.asList("Alice", "Bob", "Charlie");
names.stream()
     .map(String::toUpperCase)  // har naam ko uppercase karo
     .forEach(System.out::println); // Output: ALICE, BOB, CHARLIE
```
**Yaad rakh:** `map` = **badlo** — ek cheez ko doosri cheez mein convert karo

---

**📊 sorted() — Sorting (Slide 8)**
```java
List<Integer> nums = Arrays.asList(5, 3, 8, 1);
nums.stream()
    .sorted()
    .forEach(System.out::println); // Output: 1, 3, 5, 8
```

---

### 🏁 3.2 TERMINAL Operations (Result Dete Hain — Stream Khatam!)

Slide 9 ki full table — **FCR-CMM-AAn** (ForEach, Collect, Reduce, Count, Min, Max, AnyMatch, AllMatch, NoneMatch):

| Method | Kya karta hai |
|---|---|
| `forEach()` | Har element pe kuch karo (print etc.) |
| `collect()` | Stream ko List/Set/Map mein convert karo |
| `reduce()` | Sab elements ko ek value mein compress karo |
| `count()` | Count karo kitne elements hain |
| `min()` | Sabse chota dhundho |
| `max()` | Sabse bada dhundho |
| `anyMatch()` | Koi ek bhi match karta hai? |
| `allMatch()` | Sab match karte hain? |
| `noneMatch()` | Koi bhi match nahi karta? |

---

### 📌 Terminal Operations — Code Examples

**📦 collect() — List Mein Wapas Daalo (Slide 10)**
```java
List<String> names = Arrays.asList("Alice", "Bob", "Charlie");
List<String> uppercaseNames = names.stream()
                                   .map(String::toUpperCase)
                                   .collect(Collectors.toList()); // Stream → List
System.out.println(uppercaseNames); // Output: [ALICE, BOB, CHARLIE]
```
**Yaad rakh:** `collect(Collectors.toList())` = Stream ko wapas List banao

---

**➕ reduce() — Sab Ko Ek Mein Milao (Slide 10)**
```java
List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3, 4, 5);
int sum = numbers.stream()
                 .reduce(0, Integer::sum); // 0 = starting value
System.out.println(sum); // Output: 15
```
**Yaad rakh:** `reduce(identity, accumulator)` — identity = starting value (sum ke liye 0, multiply ke liye 1)

---

**🔝 max() — Maximum Nikalo (Slide 11)**
```java
List<Integer> numbers = Arrays.asList(10, 5, 8, 20);
int max = numbers.stream()
                 .max(Integer::compare)
                 .get(); // max() Optional return karta hai, isliye .get()
System.out.println(max); // Output: 20
```
⚠️ **Important:** `max()` aur `min()` **Optional** return karte hain — `.get()` lagana padega!

